(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the scientific methodology of the Ecological Footprint and Biocapacity, including the calculation of Global Hectares \(gha\) and ecological deficits.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Methodology of Ecological Footprint, Biocapacity, and Ecological Accounting:) Tj
T*
(   1. Ecological Footprint \(EF\) Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Developed by Mathis Wackernagel and William Rees, the Ecological Footprint measures the total) Tj
T*
(   area of biologically productive land and water required to produce all the resources an) Tj
T*
(   individual, population, or activity consumes and to absorb the waste generated \(notably carbon) Tj
T*
(   dioxide\), utilizing prevailing technology.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   EF = Sum_i [ \(Consumption_i / World_Yield_i\) * Equivalence_Factor_i ]) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
(   - Consumption_i is the total mass of resource i consumed per year.) Tj
T*
(   - World_Yield_i is the global average annual yield for resource i.) Tj
T*
(   - Equivalence_Factor_i \(EQF\) converts the specific land category \(cropland, forest, grazing,) Tj
T*
(   fishing grounds, built-up land, carbon land\) into global average productive hectares \(global) Tj
T*
(   hectares, gha\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Biocapacity \(BC\) Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   BC = Sum_j [ Area_j * Yield_Factor_j * Equivalence_Factor_j ]) Tj
T*
(   Where Yield Factor \(YF\) accounts for the local productivity of a specific country's land) Tj
T*
(   relative to world average yield for that land category.) Tj
T*
(   4. Ecological Deficit vs Ecological Reserve:) Tj
T*
