(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the chemical composition, fractionation, and physicochemical functions of Soil Organic Matter \(SOM\) and humic substances.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Soil Organic Matter \(SOM\) Composition, Humification, and Humic Chemistry:) Tj
T*
(   1. Composition and Humification Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   Soil organic matter comprises living biomass \(microbes, roots\), labile detritus \(proteins,) Tj
T*
(   carbohydrates, lipids\), and stabilized humus. Humification is the secondary synthesis of) Tj
T*
(   polycondensed, aromatic macromolecular complexes resistant to microbial enzymatic breakdown.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fractionation of Humic Substances:) Tj
T*
(   Based on solubility in acids and alkalis, humus is fractionated into three major pools:) Tj
T*
(   - Fulvic Acid: Soluble in both alkali \(0.1 M NaOH\) and strong acid \(pH 1\). Characterized by) Tj
T*
(   lowest molecular weight \(1,000-5,000 Da\), high oxygen content, and dense aliphatic carboxyl) Tj
T*
(   groups. Highly mobile and chemically reactive in chelating metal ions.) Tj
T*
(   - Humic Acid: Soluble in dilute alkali, but precipitates as dark flocs upon acidification below) Tj
T*
(   pH 2. Intermediate molecular weight \(10,000-100,000 Da\), rich in aromatic rings, phenolic) Tj
T*
(   hydroxyls, and conjugated chromophores.) Tj
T*
(   - Humin: Insoluble in both aqueous alkali and acid. Highest molecular weight \(> 100,000 Da\),) Tj
T*
(   tightly complexed with clay minerals via organo-mineral bridges.) Tj
T*
(   3. Ecological and Soil Physical Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Nutrient Reservoirs: Mineralization slowly releases essential N, P, and S.) Tj
T*
(   - Soil Structural Stabilization: Humic polymers bind mineral particles into water-stable) Tj
T*
(   micro-aggregates, improving porosity, infiltration, and root aeration.) Tj
T*
(   - Buffering & Chelation: Chelate toxic Al3+ and micronutrients \(Fe, Zn\), preventing) Tj
T*
(   precipitation and plant deficiency.) Tj
T*
