(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the geochemical reactions and biological kinetics responsible for Acid Mine Drainage \(AMD\), emphasizing the catalytic role of Acidithiobacillus ferrooxidans.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Geochemical Mechanisms and Bacterial Kinetics of Acid Mine Drainage \(AMD\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Pyrite Weathering Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   Acid Mine Drainage occurs when pyrite \(iron disulfide, FeS2\) is exposed to atmospheric oxygen) Tj
T*
(   and water during mining:) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 1 \(Abiotic Initiation\):) Tj
T*
(   2 FeS2 \(s\) + 7 O2 + 2 H2O -> 2 Fe2+ + 4 SO4^2- + 4 H+) Tj
T*
(   Generates dissolved ferrous iron, sulfate, and acidity.) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 2 \(Rate-Limiting Chemical Oxidation\):) Tj
T*
(   4 Fe2+ + O2 + 4 H+ -> 4 Fe3+ + 2 H2O) Tj
T*
(   At neutral pH, this reaction proceeds chemically, but as pH falls below 4.0, abiotic Fe2+) Tj
T*
(   oxidation slows dramatically.) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 3 \(Ferric Hydroxide Precipitation\):) Tj
T*
(   Fe3+ + 3 H2O <-> Fe\(OH\)3 \(s\) + 3 H+) Tj
T*
(   Forms orange-yellow ferric hydroxide \('yellow boy'\) precipitate, releasing additional protons.) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 4 \(Cyclic Propagating Attack\):) Tj
T*
