(   [Problem Statement]: Compare active chemical neutralization with passive wetland and anoxic limestone drain technologies for the remediation of Acid Mine Drainage \(AMD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Active vs. Passive Remediation Technologies for Acid Mine Drainage:) Tj
T*
(   1. Active Chemical Neutralization:) Tj
T*
(   - Process: Continuously dosing alkaline chemical reagents \(Hydrated lime Ca\(OH\)2, Quicklime) Tj
T*
(   CaO, Sodium hydroxide NaOH, or Limestone CaCO3\) into high-flow AMD streams inside engineered) Tj
T*
(   contact reactors.) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   Ca\(OH\)2 + H2SO4 -> CaSO4.2H2O \(Gypsum\) v) Tj
T*
(   Fe3+ + 3 OH- -> Fe\(OH\)3 v; Al3+ + 3 OH- -> Al\(OH\)3 v) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Highly reliable, handles extreme flow volumes and high metal loads, achieves) Tj
T*
(   rapid pH adjustment to 8.5-9.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: High ongoing operating costs, heavy energy consumption, and produces voluminous) Tj
T*
(   hazardous metal-rich hydroxide sludge requiring secondary dewatering and landfilling.) Tj
T*
(   2. Passive Remediation Systems:) Tj
T*
(   - Anoxic Limestone Drains \(ALDs\): Subsurface trenches filled with high-purity crushed limestone) Tj
T*
(   sealed from atmospheric oxygen. Dissolved bicarbonate neutralizes acidity: CaCO3 + H+ <-> Ca2+) Tj
T*
(   + HCO3-. Absence of oxygen prevents premature oxidation of Fe2+ to Fe3+, preventing limestone) Tj
T*
(   passivation by ferric hydroxide armoring.) Tj
T*
(   - Aerobic Constructed Wetlands: Shallow reed beds that facilitate oxygenation, allowing Fe\(OH\)3) Tj
T*
(   and MnO2 precipitation, followed by settling.) Tj
T*
(   - Anaerobic Sulfate-Reducing Bioreactors / Wetlands: Organic substrate \(compost, sawdust\)) Tj
T*
(   inoculated with Sulfate-Reducing Bacteria \(SRB, e.g., Desulfovibrio\):) Tj
T*
(   SO4^2- + 2 CH2O -> H2S + 2 HCO3-) Tj
T*
(   H2S gas precipitates divalent metals as highly stable, insoluble metal sulfides \(FeS, ZnS, CuS,) Tj
T*
(   PbS v\), permanently sequestering contaminants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
