(   - Clay mineral surfaces carry negative charges balanced by an electrostatic swarm of) Tj
T*
(   exchangeable cations extending into the pore water \(Diffuse Double Layer\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divalent cations \(Ca2+, Mg2+\) have higher charge and smaller hydrated radii, compressing the) Tj
T*
(   DDL close to the clay surface. This allows short-range attractive London-van der Waals forces) Tj
T*
(   to overcome electrostatic repulsion, causing clay platelets to flocculate into stable) Tj
T*
(   micro-aggregates.) Tj
T*
(   - In sodic soils, monovalent Na+ ions have a single positive charge and a very large hydrated) Tj
T*
(   radius \(low charge density\). This expands the DDL extensively.) Tj
T*
(   - When rainwater enters sodic soil, osmotic hydration causes adjacent clay platelets to repel) Tj
T*
(   each other vigorously, leading to complete aggregate disintegration \(colloidal dispersion\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dispersed clay particles migrate into soil pores, forming an impermeable surface seal) Tj
T*
(   \(hardpan crust\) that reduces infiltration and root respiration.) Tj
