/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Provide a rigorous quantitative formulation of the chemical reactions, gypsum requirement \(GR\), and leaching kinetics required for reclaiming sodic soils.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Quantitative Chemistry and Engineering Methodology for Sodic Soil Reclamation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Chemical Exchange Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   Reclaiming sodic soil requires replacing adsorbed Na+ with divalent Ca2+, followed by leaching) Tj
T*
(   displaced sodium salts below the root zone. Calcium sulfate dihydrate \(Gypsum, CaSO4.2H2O,) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Weight = 172.17 g/mol, Equivalent Weight = 86.08 g/eq\) is the standard industrial) Tj
T*
(   amendment:) Tj
T*
(   2 Na+_adsorbed + CaSO4 \(aq\) <-> Ca2+_adsorbed + Na2SO4 \(aq\)) Tj
T*
(   The soluble Na2SO4 is subsequently flushed out using drainage water.) Tj
T*
(   2. Theoretical Gypsum Requirement \(GR\) Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   GR \(in meq Ca2+ per 100g soil\) = \(ESP_initial - ESP_target\) * CEC / 100) Tj
T*
(   Where CEC is measured in meq/100g.) Tj
T*
(   To calculate field application in Metric Tons of pure gypsum per hectare:) Tj
T*
(   - Mass of topsoil \(plow layer depth d = 0.15 m, bulk density rho_b = 1.33 Mg/m3, area A =) Tj
T*
(   10,000 m2\):) Tj
T*
(   Soil Mass = A * d * rho_b = 10,000 * 0.15 * 1.33 = 2,000 Metric Tons = 2.0 * 10^9 g.) Tj
T*
(   - Pure Gypsum Mass = [ GR \(meq/100g\) / 100 ] * Equivalent Weight of Gypsum \(86.08 mg/meq\) *) Tj
T*
(   Total Soil Mass \(g\) / 10^9 mg/ton.) Tj
T*
(   - Simplified Engineering Formula:) Tj
T*
(   GR \(tons/ha\) = 0.8608 * [ \(ESP_initial - ESP_target\) * CEC / 100 ] * \(Soil Mass in 10^6 kg\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Leaching Requirement and Soil Structure Stabilization:) Tj
T*
(   Applying gypsum elevates electrolyte concentration in the soil solution, temporarily preventing) Tj
T*
(   clay dispersion during the initial leaching phase until calcium fully saturates exchange sites.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
