(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Universal Soil Loss Equation \(USLE\), define every component factor, and analyze erosion control management strategies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Universal Soil Loss Equation \(USLE\) and Erosion Control Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Model \(Wischmeier and Smith\):) Tj
T*
(   A = R * K * LS * C * P) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
(   - A: Average annual predicted soil loss per unit area, typically expressed in metric tons per) Tj
T*
(   hectare per year \(t/ha/yr\).) Tj
T*
(   - R: Rainfall and Runoff Erosivity Factor. Quantifies the kinetic energy of raindrops and the) Tj
T*
(   peak intensity of runoff \(EI30 index, product of total storm kinetic energy E and maximum) Tj
T*
