/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the physics of Wind Erosion, differentiating between Saltation, Suspension, and Surface Creep, and formulate aerodynamic mitigation measures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Aerodynamics and Mechanics of Wind Erosion:) Tj
T*
(   1. Wind Shear Stress and Threshold Friction Velocity:) Tj
T*
(   Wind erosion initiates when surface wind velocity generates a boundary-layer friction velocity) Tj
T*
(   \(u*\) that exceeds the critical threshold friction velocity \(u*_t\) required to overcome particle) Tj
T*
(   gravity and inter-particle cohesion:) Tj
T*
(   u*_t = A_const * sqrt[ \(\(rho_p - rho_a\) * g * d\) / rho_a ]) Tj
T*
(   Where rho_p is particle density, rho_a is air density, g is gravity, and d is grain diameter.) Tj
T*
(   2. Three Modes of Particle Transport:) Tj
T*
(   - Saltation \(50% to 70% of Total Wind Transport\): Medium-sized sand grains \(0.1 mm to 0.5 mm) Tj
T*
(   diameter\) are lifted briefly into the airflow by aerodynamic lift and Magnus forces, travel) Tj
T*
(   downwind in parabolic trajectories, and impact the soil surface. Their ballistic impacts knock) Tj
T*
(   other particles into motion, creating a cascading avalanche effect.) Tj
T*
(   - Suspension \(3% to 15% of Transport\): Fine particles \(< 0.1 mm, silt and clay\) launched into) Tj
T*
(   the air by saltation impacts. Due to low terminal settling velocities, vertical aerodynamic) Tj
T*
(   turbulence carries them high into the troposphere, transporting them hundreds or thousands of) Tj
T*
(   kilometers as dust storms.) Tj
T*
(   - Surface Creep \(5% to 25% of Transport\): Coarse sand grains \(0.5 mm to 2.0 mm diameter\) too) Tj
T*
(   heavy to be lifted off the ground. They are slowly rolled and pushed forward along the soil) Tj
T*
(   surface by the continuous bombardment of saltating grains.) Tj
T*
(   3. Aerodynamic Mitigation Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   - Shelterbelts and Windbreaks: Multi-row belts of deciduous and evergreen trees planted) Tj
T*
(   perpendicular to prevailing winds. A properly designed windbreak reduces wind velocity up to 30) Tj
T*
(   to 40 times its height downwind.) Tj
T*
(   - Conservation Tillage & Surface Residue: Retaining crop stubble increases surface aerodynamic) Tj
T*
(   roughness \(z0\), shifting the zero-velocity plane upward and sheltering erodible grains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
