(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mining Impacts on Land Systems and Mine Spoil Rehabilitation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical and Chemical Disturbance:) Tj
T*
(   - Topsoil Stripping & Overburden Dumps: Large-scale open-cast mining removes entire biological) Tj
T*
(   ecosystems, stripping fertile topsoil horizons and dumping unweathered overburden rock in vast) Tj
T*
(   unstable spoil heaps prone to landslides and erosion.) Tj
T*
(   - Subsidence & Hydrological Disruption: Underground mining creates subterranean voids leading) Tj
T*
(   to surface subsidence, damaging buildings, fracturing shallow aquifers, and diverting surface) Tj
T*
(   streams into underground mine pools.) Tj
T*
(   - Toxic Tailings & Acid Generation: Flotation tailings contain fine-ground mineral gangue,) Tj
T*
(   residual reagents \(cyanide, xanthates\), and heavy metals \(As, Cd, Pb\), generating chronic) Tj
T*
(   leachate contamination.) Tj
T*
(   2. Ecological Spoil Rehabilitation Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1: Geotechnical Re-grading & Slope Stabilization: Re-grading steep spoil banks to safe) Tj
T*
(   angles \(< 18 to 20 degrees\), installing contour berms and riprap rock chutes to channel) Tj
T*
(   stormwater safely.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2: Topsoil Replacement or Technosol Synthesis: Spreading stockpiled topsoil \(0.3 to 0.5) Tj
T*
(   m depth\). If topsoil is depleted, synthesize technosols using organic compost, municipal) Tj
T*
(   biosolids, and crushed limestone to buffer acidity.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3: Pioneer Revegetation with Nitrogen-Fixing Species: Seeding hardy pioneer grass) Tj
T*
(   species \(Cynodon dactylon, Vetiveria zizanioides\) and leguminous shrubs/trees \(Leucaena) Tj
T*
(   leucocephala, Acacia mangium\) inoculated with Rhizobium and Arbuscular Mycorrhizal Fungi \(AMF\)) Tj
T*
(   to build soil organic matter.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 4: Secondary Ecological Succession: Introducing indigenous climax forest trees to) Tj
T*
(   establish self-sustaining biodiversity.) Tj
T*
