(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the physiological and genetic adaptations of Heavy Metal Hyperaccumulators, discussing metal transporter families and vacuolar sequestration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Physiological and Molecular Architecture of Metal Hyperaccumulation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Hyperaccumulators \(Baker and Brooks Thresholds\):) Tj
T*
(   Plants that naturally accumulate and tolerate toxic metals in their dry shoot biomass without) Tj
T*
(   exhibiting toxicity symptoms:) Tj
T*
(   - > 100 mg/kg dry mass for Cadmium \(Cd\) and Selenium \(Se\).) Tj
T*
(   - > 1,000 mg/kg dry mass for Nickel \(Ni\), Copper \(Cu\), Cobalt \(Co\), and Lead \(Pb\).) Tj
T*
(   - > 10,000 mg/kg dry mass for Zinc \(Zn\) and Manganese \(Mn\).) Tj
T*
(   Model hyperaccumulators include Noccaea caerulescens \(Zn/Cd/Ni\) and Alyssum bertolonii \(Ni\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Key Membrane Transporter Superfamilies:) Tj
T*
(   - ZIP Family \(ZRT/IRT-like Proteins\): High-affinity zinc and iron transporters expressed at the) Tj
T*
(   root plasma membrane, driving rapid influx of divalent cations from the soil solution.) Tj
T*
(   - HMA Family \(Heavy Metal P1B-type ATPases\): HMA4 and HMA2 are constitutively overexpressed in) Tj
T*
(   hyperaccumulators, actively pumping Cd2+ and Zn2+ across the pericycle plasma membrane into the) Tj
T*
(   xylem vessels for rapid shoot translocation.) Tj
T*
(   - NRAMP Family \(Natural Resistance-Associated Macrophage Proteins\): Mediate divalent metal ion) Tj
T*
(   export across the tonoplast or uptake across membranes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Intracellular Chelation and Vacuolar Compartmentation:) Tj
T*
(   - In the cytosol, free heavy metals induce cellular oxidative stress and disrupt enzyme active) Tj
T*
(   sites. Hyperaccumulators synthesize high concentrations of non-protein chelators:) Tj
T*
(   Phytochelatins [poly\(gamma-glutamyl-cysteinyl\)glycine], Metallothioneins \(cysteine-rich) Tj
T*
(   polypeptides\), and organic acids \(histidine, nicotianamine, malate\).) Tj
T*
(   - Metal-chelate complexes are translocated into the central plant vacuole via ABC transporters) Tj
T*
(   \(such as HMT1, ABCC1\) and metal/H+ antiporters \(CAX, MTP1\), sequestering the toxic ions) Tj
T*
(   permanently away from sensitive cytoplasmic metabolic machinery.) Tj
