(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the chemical and physical principles of Ex-situ Soil Washing for heavy metal and organic decontamination, including wash water recovery.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ex-Situ Soil Washing Technology and Process Chemistry:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Physical and Chemical Principles:) Tj
T*
(   - Soil washing is a water-based volume-reduction process that physically separates fine soil) Tj
T*
(   fractions \(clays and silts\) from coarse fractions \(sand and gravel\), or chemically extracts) Tj
T*
(   contaminants into aqueous solution using chemical lixiviants.) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrophobic organics and heavy metals preferentially partition onto the surface of fine clay) Tj
T*
(   and organic humus particles due to their high specific surface area and cation exchange sites.) Tj
T*
(   2. Multi-Stage Process Flowsheet:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1 \(Mechanical Pre-treatment\): Excavated soil is passed through vibrating trommels and) Tj
T*
(   screens \(grizzlies\) to remove oversized rocks and construction debris \(> 50 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2 \(Attrition Scrubbing\): Soil is slurried with water \(20-40% solids\) in high-energy) Tj
T*
(   attrition scrubbers. Intensive particle-particle scouring abrades the contaminant-laden fine) Tj
T*
(   coatings off coarse quartz sand grains.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3 \(Hydrocyclone Classification\): Centrifugal separation in hydrocyclones separates) Tj
T*
(   clean coarse sand \(underflow\) from the fine clay/silt slurry \(overflow\). Coarse sand is clean) Tj
T*
(   and backfilled directly on site.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 4 \(Chemical Extraction\): The fine slurry is transferred to stirred leaching reactors) Tj
T*
(   containing chemical washing reagents:) Tj
T*
(   * Heavy Metal Extraction: Chelating agents \(0.01 to 0.05 M Disodium EDTA, citric acid, or) Tj
T*
(   gluconic acid\) forming soluble metal-chelate complexes: M2+ + EDTA^4- -> [M-EDTA]^2-.) Tj
T*
(   * Organic Extraction: Non-ionic surfactants \(Triton X-100, Tween-80\) at concentrations) Tj
T*
(   exceeding Critical Micelle Concentration \(CMC\) to solubilize PAHs into micellar cores.) Tj
T*
(   3. Wash Water Treatment and Reagent Recovery:) Tj
T*
(   - The laden extractant is separated from the residual fine cake via membrane filter presses.) Tj
T*
(   - Heavy metals are recovered by dropping pH to 1.5-2.0 to dissociate the EDTA complex,) Tj
T*
(   precipitating metals as sulfides \(Na2S\) or through electrochemical deposition, allowing EDTA) Tj
T*
(   regeneration and 95% water recycling.) Tj
T*
