(   \(HNO3\).) Tj
T*
(   - When hydronium ions \(H3O+\) enter the soil solution, they compete for negative cation exchange) Tj
T*
(   sites on clay minerals and humus:) Tj
T*
(   Colloid-[Ca2+, Mg2+, K+] + 2 H+ <-> Colloid-[2 H+] + Ca2+ + Mg2+ + 2 K+) Tj
T*
(   - The displaced basic cations enter the soil pore solution. Because mobile companion anions) Tj
T*
(   \(SO4^2- and NO3-\) cannot be retained by negatively charged soil colloids, they leach down the) Tj
T*
