(   2. Aluminum Mobilization and Root Toxicity:) Tj
T*
(   - In neutral soils, aluminum exists as insoluble, non-toxic aluminosilicates and gibbsite) Tj
T*
(   [Al\(OH\)3].) Tj
T*
(   - As soil pH falls below 5.0 \(and especially < 4.5\), aluminum precipitates dissolve, releasing) Tj
T*
(   toxic monomeric trivalent aluminum ions:) Tj
T*
(   Al\(OH\)3 \(s\) + 3 H+ <-> Al3+ \(aq\) + 3 H2O) Tj
T*
(   - Al3+ is a potent phytotoxin. It binds to pectin carboxyl groups in root cell walls, disrupts) Tj
T*
(   root plasma membrane integrity, and inhibits Ca2+ influx and beta-glucan synthesis, arresting) Tj
T*
(   root tip mitotic division. The root system becomes stunted, stubby, and incapable of water and) Tj
T*
(   nutrient uptake.) Tj
T*
(   3. Agricultural and Forest Liming:) Tj
T*
(   - Applying finely ground agricultural limestone \(CaCO3\) or dolomitic limestone [CaMg\(CO3\)2]:) Tj
T*
(   CaCO3 + 2 H+ -> Ca2+ + H2O + CO2) Tj
T*
(   Al3+ + 3 H2O + 3 OH- -> Al\(OH\)3 \(s\) v) Tj
T*
(   - Neutralizes free acidity, raises soil pH above 5.5, precipitates toxic Al3+ as inert) Tj
T*
(   hydroxide, and replenishes depleted exchangeable Ca2+ and Mg2+.) Tj
