(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the chemical mechanisms of Phosphate Fixation in acidic versus calcareous soils, and discuss the role of Arbuscular Mycorrhizal Fungi \(AMF\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Phosphate Chemistry, Fixation Equilibria, and Mycorrhizal Solubilization:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Soil Phosphate Dilemma:) Tj
T*
(   Phosphorus is a critical macronutrient, but orthophosphate ions \(H2PO4- and HPO4^2-\) exhibit) Tj
T*
(   extreme reactivity in soils, rapidly forming insoluble chemical precipitates or chemisorbing) Tj
T*
(   onto mineral surfaces, leaving less than 0.1% of total soil P in plant-available solution.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fixation in Acid Soils \(pH < 5.5\):) Tj
T*
(   - Chemisorption: Orthophosphate ions adsorb onto hydrated iron and aluminum sesquioxides) Tj
T*
(   \(gibbsite, goethite\) by displacing surface hydroxyls in ligand exchange reactions, forming) Tj
T*
(   stable binuclear inner-sphere complexes:) Tj
T*
(   -Fe-OH + H2PO4- -> -Fe-H2PO4 + OH-) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Precipitation: High dissolved Al3+ and Fe3+ concentrations precipitate insoluble) Tj
T*
(   minerals:) Tj
T*
(   Al3+ + H2PO4- + 2 H2O <-> AlPO4.2H2O \(Variscite\) v) Tj
T*
(   Fe3+ + H2PO4- + 2 H2O <-> FePO4.2H2O \(Strengite\) v) Tj
T*
(   3. Fixation in Calcareous / Alkaline Soils \(pH > 7.5\):) Tj
T*
(   - In soils containing abundant calcium carbonate \(CaCO3\), soluble monocalcium phosphate) Tj
T*
(   converts stepwise into increasingly insoluble calcium phosphate minerals:) Tj
T*
(   Dicalcium phosphate \(CaHPO4\) -> Tricalcium phosphate [Ca3\(PO4\)2] -> Carbonate-hydroxylapatite) Tj
T*
(   [Ca10\(PO4,CO3\)6\(OH\)2].) Tj
T*
(   - Optimal phosphate availability occurs within a narrow pH window between 6.0 and 7.0.) Tj
T*
(   4. Role of Arbuscular Mycorrhizal Fungi \(AMF\):) Tj
T*
(   - Glomeromycota fungi establish mutualistic symbioses with plant root cortical cells, forming) Tj
T*
(   branched arbuscules.) Tj
T*
(   - AMF hyphae extend far beyond the root nutrient depletion zone \(increasing effective soil) Tj
T*
