(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the biochemical transformations of Nitrogen in the pedosphere, including Biological Nitrogen Fixation, Nitrification, and Denitrification pathways.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biochemical Nitrogen Cycle: Fixation, Nitrification, and Denitrification Pathways:) Tj
T*
(   1. Biological Nitrogen Fixation \(BNF\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mediated by prokaryotes possessing the nitrogenase enzyme complex:) Tj
T*
(   N2 + 8 H+ + 8 e- + 16 MgATP -> 2 NH3 + H2 + 16 MgADP + 16 Pi) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Components:) Tj
T*
(   * Fe-Protein \(Dinitrogenase reductase\): A homodimer with a [4Fe-4S] cluster; hydrolyzes ATP to) Tj
T*
(   transfer electrons to the catalytic component.) Tj
T*
(   * MoFe-Protein \(Dinitrogenase\): An alpha2-beta2 tetramer containing the P-cluster [8Fe-7S] and) Tj
T*
(   FeMo-cofactor [7Fe-9S-Mo-X-homocitrate], binding and reducing N2.) Tj
T*
(   - Symbiotic Associations: Rhizobium/Bradyrhizobium with legumes, Frankia with actinorhizal) Tj
T*
(   trees; Free-living diazotrophs: Azotobacter \(aerobic\), Clostridium \(anaerobic\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Two-Step Autotrophic Nitrification:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Ammonium Oxidation \(Nitrosomonas, Nitrosococcus\):) Tj
T*
(   2 NH4+ + 3 O2 -> 2 NO2- + 4 H+ + 2 H2O + Energy) Tj
T*
(   Catalyzed by membrane-bound Ammonia Monooxygenase \(AMO\) and Hydroxylamine Oxidoreductase \(HAO\).) Tj
T*
(   Releases 2 protons per NH4+, causing natural soil acidification.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Nitrite Oxidation \(Nitrobacter, Nitrospira\):) Tj
T*
(   2 NO2- + O2 -> 2 NO3- + Energy) Tj
T*
(   Catalyzed by Nitrite Oxidoreductase \(NXR\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Anaerobic Denitrification:) Tj
T*
(   - Carried out by facultative heterotrophic bacteria \(Pseudomonas stutzeri, Paracoccus) Tj
T*
(   denitrificans\) when soil oxygen falls below 10% \(waterlogged conditions\):) Tj
T*
(   NO3- \(Nitrate\) -> NO2- \(Nitrite\) -> NO \(Nitric oxide\) -> N2O \(Nitrous oxide\) -> N2 \(Dinitrogen) Tj
T*
(   gas\)) Tj
T*
(   - Serves as terminal electron acceptors in anaerobic respiration. Incomplete reduction results) Tj
T*
(   in emissions of nitrous oxide \(N2O\), a potent greenhouse gas with a Global Warming Potential) Tj
T*
(   273 times that of CO2.) Tj
T*
