(   [Problem Statement]: Define Sustainable Land Management \(SLM\), and evaluate Agroforestry as an engineering system for optimizing soil carbon stocks and hydrology.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sustainable Land Management \(SLM\) and Agroforestry Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Framework of SLM:) Tj
T*
(   Defined by the UN Food and Agriculture Organization \(FAO\) as: 'The use of land resources,) Tj
T*
(   including soils, water, animals and plants, for the production of goods to meet changing human) Tj
T*
(   needs, while simultaneously ensuring the long-term productive potential of these resources and) Tj
T*
(   the maintenance of their environmental functions.') Tj
T*
(   2. Agroforestry as an Integrated Engineering System:) Tj
T*
(   Agroforestry deliberately integrates woody perennials \(trees, shrubs\) with agricultural crops) Tj
T*
(   and/or livestock on the same land-management unit:) Tj
T*
(   - Silvoarable Systems: Alley cropping where food crops are cultivated between rows of hedgerow) Tj
T*
(   trees \(e.g., Gliricidia sepium, Leucaena\).) Tj
T*
