/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate a mathematical model for ecosystem Carrying Capacity \(K\), and solve for sustainable herbivore stocking density in a managed rangeland.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mathematical Modeling of Ecosystem Carrying Capacity \(K\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Formulation \(Verhulst-Pearl Logistic Growth\):) Tj
T*
(   dN/dt = r * N * [ \(K - N\) / K ]) Tj
T*
(   Where N is population size, r is intrinsic per capita growth rate, and K is carrying capacity) Tj
T*
(   \(the environmental asymptote where population growth equals zero\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Resource-Based Carrying Capacity Formulation for Rangeland:) Tj
T*
(   Carrying Capacity \(K\) can be determined directly from Primary Biomass Energy Balance:) Tj
T*
(   K = \(A * Y_forage * U_factor\) / \(I_annual\)) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
(   - A: Total usable grazing area \(hectares, ha\).) Tj
T*
(   - Y_forage: Total annual above-ground primary forage production \(kg dry matter/ha/yr\).) Tj
T*
(   - U_factor: Proper Use Factor \(allowable harvest efficiency without causing pasture) Tj
T*
(   degradation, typically 0.40 to 0.50, adhering to the 'take-half-and-leave-half' principle\).) Tj
T*
(   - I_annual: Total annual dry matter forage consumption per animal unit \(AU\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Solved Numerical Engineering Case Study:) Tj
T*
(   - Given:) Tj
T*
(   * Managed rangeland area A = 2,500 hectares.) Tj
T*
(   * Annual edible forage yield Y_forage = 1,800 kg DM/ha/yr.) Tj
T*
(   * Proper use factor U_factor = 0.40 \(40% allowable consumption\).) Tj
T*
(   * Standard Animal Unit \(AU = 450 kg beef cow\) daily dry matter intake = 2.5% of body mass =) Tj
T*
(   11.25 kg DM/day.) Tj
T*
(   * Annual intake per AU: I_annual = 11.25 kg/day * 365 days = 4,106.25 kg DM/yr.) Tj
T*
(   - Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   * Total annual forage produced = 2,500 ha * 1,800 kg/ha/yr = 4,500,000 kg DM/yr.) Tj
T*
(   * Allowable sustainable forage harvest = 4,500,000 * 0.40 = 1,800,000 kg DM/yr.) Tj
T*
(   * Maximum Sustainable Carrying Capacity K = 1,800,000 kg / 4,106.25 kg/AU/yr = 438.35 Animal) Tj
T*
(   Units.) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Recommendation: The rangeland can sustainably support a maximum stocking density) Tj
T*
(   of 438 Animal Units \(or 0.175 AU/ha\) without triggering soil compaction, vegetative) Tj
T*
(   degradation, or accelerated erosion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
