(   Corporate GHG Protocol Accounting: Scope 1, 2, and 3 Carbon Footprinting:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Classification under the GHG Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   Established by the World Resources Institute \(WRI\) and the World Business Council for) Tj
T*
(   Sustainable Development \(WBCSD\), greenhouse gas emissions are categorized into three reporting) Tj
T*
(   scopes:) Tj
T*
(   - Scope 1 \(Direct GHG Emissions\):) Tj
T*
(   Emissions from sources that are owned or controlled by the reporting organization:) Tj
T*
(   * Stationary combustion: Boilers, furnaces, gas turbines combusting natural gas, diesel, or) Tj
T*
(   coal for facility heat and steam generation.) Tj
T*
(   * Mobile combustion: Company-owned fleet vehicles.) Tj
T*
(   * Process emissions: Chemical or biological transformations, such as direct CO2 or CH4) Tj
T*
(   outgassing from large-scale industrial fermentation bioreactors and anaerobic digesters.) Tj
T*
(   * Fugitive emissions: Refrigerant leaks \(HFCs\) from cold storage facilities and) Tj
T*
(   air-conditioning chillers.) Tj
T*
(   - Scope 2 \(Indirect Emissions from Purchased Energy\):) Tj
T*
(   Emissions associated with the generation of purchased electricity, steam, heating, or cooling) Tj
T*
(   consumed by the reporting company:) Tj
T*
(   * Quantified via Location-Based Method \(regional grid average emission factor\) or Market-Based) Tj
T*
(   Method \(contractual emissions from Renewable Energy Certificates RECs or Power Purchase) Tj
T*
(   Agreements PPAs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Scope 3 \(Other Indirect Value Chain Emissions\):) Tj
T*
(   All upstream and downstream emissions across the complete product lifecycle:) Tj
T*
(   * Upstream: Purchased goods and services \(e.g., carbon footprint of agricultural corn or) Tj
T*
(   sugarcane feedstock cultivation, fertilizers, synthetic enzymes\), upstream transport, business) Tj
T*
(   travel, and capital equipment.) Tj
T*
(   * Downstream: Transportation of bioproducts to retail distributors, end-of-life treatment of) Tj
T*
(   sold products \(e.g., landfill degradation or composting of bioplastics\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Significance in Biotechnology: Scope 3 emissions frequently account for 70% to 90% of total) Tj
T*
(   lifecycle emissions in bio-manufacturing, highlighting the necessity of green supply chain) Tj
T*
(   procurement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
