12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the Land Degradation Neutrality \(LDN\) framework established by the UNCCD, including its operational indicators and the 'Avoid, Reduce, Reverse' hierarchy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Land Degradation Neutrality \(LDN\) Framework under UNCCD:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Definition and Mandate:) Tj
T*
(   Formulated under the United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification \(UNCCD\) and codified) Tj
T*
(   in SDG Target 15.3, Land Degradation Neutrality is defined as:) Tj
T*
(   'A state whereby the amount and quality of land resources necessary to support ecosystem) Tj
T*
(   functions and services and enhance food security remain stable or increase within specified) Tj
T*
(   temporal and spatial scales and ecosystems.') Tj
T*
(   The fundamental objective is to balance any unavoidable land degradation with equivalent) Tj
T*
(   ecological restoration \('No Net Loss' of natural capital\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The 'One Out, All Out' Operational Indicators:) Tj
T*
(   National progress toward LDN is evaluated using three complementary, biophysical) Tj
T*
(   sub-indicators:) Tj
T*
(   - Land Cover / Land Cover Change: Tracks transitions from natural and productive ecosystems) Tj
T*
(   \(forests, wetlands\) to artificial, urbanized, or degraded surfaces using remote sensing.) Tj
T*
(   - Land Productivity Dynamics \(LPD\): Measures Net Primary Productivity \(NPP\) trajectories) Tj
T*
(   derived from satellite Normalized Difference Vegetation Index \(NDVI\) time-series.) Tj
T*
(   - Carbon Stocks \(Soil Organic Carbon\): Assesses changes in soil organic carbon \(SOC\) in the top) Tj
T*
(   30 cm layer \(expressed in tons C/ha\).) Tj
T*
ET

