12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate circular bio-refinery engineering strategies for valorizing lignocellulosic agricultural residues into biofuels, biochemicals, and soil amendments.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Circular Bio-Refinery Engineering: Valorization of Lignocellulosic Waste Streams:) Tj
T*
(   1. Composition of Lignocellulosic Agricultural Residues:) Tj
T*
(   Crop residues \(rice straw, wheat straw, sugarcane bagasse, corn stover\) represent abundant) Tj
T*
(   renewable biomass composed of three biopolymers: Cellulose \(35-50%, crystalline) Tj
T*
(   beta-1,4-glucan\), Hemicellulose \(20-35%, branched heteropolysaccharide containing xylose,) Tj
T*
(   arabinose\), and Lignin \(15-25%, complex aromatic polymer of phenylpropane units\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Cascading Fractionation and Upgrading Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   A modern circular bio-refinery replaces the linear open-field burning of crop residue with) Tj
T*
(   multi-product valorization:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Green Pre-treatment:) Tj
T*
(   Hydrothermal or ionic liquid / deep eutectic solvent \(DES\) pre-treatment dissolves lignin and) Tj
T*
(   hemicellulose, disrupting crystalline cellulose microfibrils without generating toxic) Tj
T*
(   fermentation inhibitors \(furfural, 5-HMF\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Enzymatic Saccharification:) Tj
T*
(   Engineered cellulase and hemicellulase enzyme cocktails hydrolyze cellulose and hemicellulose) Tj
T*
(   into hexose \(glucose\) and pentose \(xylose\) fermentable sugars at high conversion yields \(>) Tj
T*
(   90%\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Bioconversion into High-Value Biochemicals:) Tj
T*
(   Genetically modified microbial strains ferment sugars into 2nd-generation bio-ethanol, lactic) Tj
T*
(   acid \(precursor for biodegradable poly-lactic acid PLA bioplastics\), or microbial) Tj
T*
(   biosurfactants.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Lignin Upgrading to Technical Aromatic Chemicals:) Tj
T*
(   Extracted lignin is catalytic depolymerized into bio-based phenols, vanillin, and carbon) Tj
T*
(   fibers, replacing petrochemical aromatics.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Thermochemical Pyrolysis of Solid Filter Cakes:) Tj
T*
(   Residual unhydrolyzed organic filter cakes undergo slow pyrolysis to produce Biochar and) Tj
T*
(   synthesis gas. Biochar is amended back to agricultural fields to replenish soil organic carbon,) Tj
T*
(   restore CEC, and close the circular nutrient loop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
